Supporting continuity of care between professionals and services is crucial, and our solution can facilitate this through dossier-context continuity. This feature provides structured handover summaries that enable another professional or a colleague resuming a shift to efficiently take over an in-progress dossier with full context, thus ensuring seamless continuity of care.

Regarding integration with existing hospital information systems, our design principle is to embed the assistant into the staff's existing work environment and tools without introducing any rupture. This means we can integrate our solution with the client's electronic patient record (DPI) and other existing systems, ensuring a smooth workflow and minimizing disruptions.

To achieve response times compatible with daily clinical use, we will focus on optimizing the performance of our Retrieval-augmented generation model. Although the sovereign European open-weight model we offer is fully auditable and has strong grounding behavior, it may have somewhat lower raw performance on complex generative tasks compared to top-tier proprietary models. However, this trade-off is necessary to ensure explainability and sovereignty over the AI system.

By addressing these key requirements through our AI capabilities and design principles, we can provide an innovative solution that not only meets but exceeds the client's expectations in terms of efficiency, quality of care, and integration with existing systems.
